{"id":"1e0217f4-10f0-430f-a7ae-c3d7f01f79ce","revision":0,"last_node_id":43,"last_link_id":54,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-460],"size":[5000,400],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Mannequin storyboard → six shots · MOSS-Image SFT + FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nBlock the scene first, cast it after. **MOSS-Image** draws the whole storyboard as one 3 × 2 sheet with two plain mannequins — a **red** one and a **blue** one — on a grey rooftop set. **Split Grid** cuts the six panels, and every panel becomes one clip with the real characters: **red = Mei, blue = Kai**.\n\n1. **Load Media** holds the cast and the set: `# Mei`, `# Kai`, `# Place`. Three **Tree Branch** nodes take them out by name — a list of one each, which ComfyUI repeats for all six clips.\n2. The sheet prompt says who is which colour and what happens in each panel; **Split Grid** finds the gutters and returns the panels in reading order.\n3. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one structured OmniRef prompt per panel from an **Action** line and a **Sound** line. Its subject definitions carry the colour mapping: *the RED mannequin in <Picture 1> stands for <Subject 1> (Mei, <Picture 2>), the BLUE one for <Subject 2> (Kai, <Picture 3>)*. The panel is only a blocking reference — no **Add Guide**, so no mannequin reaches the film.\n4. **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**: the panel `<Picture 1>`, Mei `<Picture 2>`, Kai `<Picture 3>`, the rooftop `<Picture 4>`. 0.98 MP (1344 × 768), 124 frames (~5 s).\n5. **Construct Tree** gives the clips the panels' shape: **Video Grid** plays them as the same 3 × 2 sheet, **Save by Path** names them after the shots, **Concatenate Video** joins the film, and the **Compare Viewer** wipes each panel against its clip.\n\nKeep the colours in both places — the sheet prompt and the subject definitions — when you change the cast."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Mannequin storyboard → six shots · MOSS-Image SFT + FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nBlock the scene first, cast it after. **MOSS-Image** draws the whole storyboard as one 3 × 2 sheet with two plain mannequins — a **red** one and a **blue** one — on a grey rooftop set. **Split Grid** cuts the six panels, and every panel becomes one clip with the real characters: **red = Mei, blue = Kai**.\n\n1. **Load Media** holds the cast and the set: `# Mei`, `# Kai`, `# Place`. Three **Tree Branch** nodes take them out by name — a list of one each, which ComfyUI repeats for all six clips.\n2. The sheet prompt says who is which colour and what happens in each panel; **Split Grid** finds the gutters and returns the panels in reading order.\n3. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one structured OmniRef prompt per panel from an **Action** line and a **Sound** line. Its subject definitions carry the colour mapping: *the RED mannequin in <Picture 1> stands for <Subject 1> (Mei, <Picture 2>), the BLUE one for <Subject 2> (Kai, <Picture 3>)*. The panel is only a blocking reference — no **Add Guide**, so no mannequin reaches the film.\n4. **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**: the panel `<Picture 1>`, Mei `<Picture 2>`, Kai `<Picture 3>`, the rooftop `<Picture 4>`. 0.98 MP (1344 × 768), 124 frames (~5 s).\n5. **Construct Tree** gives the clips the panels' shape: **Video Grid** plays them as the same 3 × 2 sheet, **Save by Path** names them after the shots, **Concatenate Video** joins the film, and the **Compare Viewer** wipes each panel against its clip.\n\nKeep the colours in both places — the sheet prompt and the subject definitions — when you change the cast."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,560],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"files","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"files","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[1,2,3]},{"localized_name":"name